<title>USA: Hughes unit gets $500 mln Canadian contract.</title>
<headline>Hughes unit gets $500 mln Canadian contract.</headline>
<dateline>GOLETA, Calif. 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hughes Electronics Corp said Monday its Hughes Delco Systems Operations unit had received a development and production contract from the Canadian government to provide electric-drive turrets for an Armored Personnel Carrier.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said the subcontract calls for Hughes Delco to provide turrets for an initial 240 vehicles, with options for up to 651 vehicles.</p>
<p>If the options are exercised, the contract could be worth nearly $500 million.</p>
<p>Hughes is part of General Motors Corp.</p>
</text>
